elp arrange  senior housing for her parents until her  father passed away while she initially  remarked that her soup tasted bitter it  was fulfilling by the end of the meal  the note left by scp-348 simply said  thank you once a test was conducted  involving scp-348 and the 60 year old  man who was suffering from a terminal  illness the grandfather to many  grandchildren was offered the bowl of  soup and delightedly ate it claiming it  was the best soup he had ever tasted it  gave him a sense of satisfaction and  even eased some of the pain caused by  his illness a week later The Old Man  passed away peacefully in his sleep oh  what's that those sweet soup messages  weren't wholesome enough to encourage  even a few sobs okay then you heartless  little monster we'll step up our game  with scp-3017 now you might be forgiven  for thinking that this is a particular  literally monstrous SCP after all that  is his anomalous effect Fraser melbrook  is or rather was an otherwise ordinary  man Afflicted with an infectious Cognito  Hazard this would alter the perception  of anyone around Frasier or any person  who might have spoken to him and made  them believe that he belonged in custody  people would be compelled to think that  Frasier was a dangerous violent  individual but with no actual proof that  he was in many cases anyone exposed to  his Cognito Hazard would even try to  lock him up themselves the one reprieve  however was that a number of Frazier's  immediate family and close friends were  immune to this effect either this was  through experiencing prolonged exposure  to scp-3017 or by simply knowing him  well enough to have context that  canceled out the false beliefs that he  was a violent criminal with an extensive  record designated as  scp-3017-1s the people closest to him  remain unaffected Fraser was able to  maintain healthy relationships with all  of them until scp-3017 fell into the  hands of the foundation arrested and  placed in containment thanks to the  anomalous effects of scp-3017 the  foundation believed that Fraser Mel  Brook had close ties and connections to  multiple groups of Interest they began  to relentlessly torturously interrogate  Frasier threatening his family unless he  gave them the answers to their questions  information that he simply could not  provide he hadn't even heard of the  geois the foundation wanted to know  about let alone had any direct  affiliation with them but still they  kept pressing him keeping him locked up  and not allowing him to see his family  even when his grandmother developed lung  cancer treated with suspicion and  hostility non-stop every day  scp-3017 would get one last shot at  freedom however researcher Rylan who had  been studying Frazier's anomalous  properties as well as a security officer  that had been a signed to watch melbrook  both developed the same immunity to the  prisoner's Cognito Hazard as his family  and friends had working together they  were able to Spring scp-3017 from  Foundation custody and Rylan took him  back home to see his family little did  either of them know of the tragedy that  awaited them in a cruel twist of fate a  house fire had set melbrook's family  home Ablaze claiming the lives of his  parents both brothers his sister  grandmother and even his fiancee utterly  devastated and overwhelmed with grief  the loss of his loved ones completely  broke Frazier he had spent so much of  his life persecuted accused of heinous  crimes and arrested despite being  completely innocent and as if that  wasn't bad enough he'd fought his way  free from the foundation only to find  his home reduced to Ash the day before  he made it back by the time the SCP  Foundation arrived to recapture him it  was already too late Frasier was dead  and researcher Ryland turned herself  over without resistance the foundation  soon realized what they had done how  they had tortured an innocent man who  didn't actually have the information  they thought he did in quiet shame they  reclassified scp-3017 under a new object  class neutralized feeling tyria maybe a  little moist around the eyes oh those  are just your allergies oh yeah of  course they are how could we be so silly  alright let's move on taking a step back  from Grim dark reality for a moment  let's instead delve into a world of  fantasy  scp-1762 was a seemingly ordinary  cardboard box spray painted silver with  the words here be dragons written on it  in permanent marker usually it remained  empty but would occasionally open  releasing dozens of tiny origami dragons  that would fly out after black smoke had  plumed out of the box it was no doubt a  sight to behold the kind of Fantastical  occurrence that is inherently filled  with childlike wonder often a written or  carved message would be left behind  after the origami dragons flew back into  their box and this is how the foundation  was able to learn of the terrible  misfortune known as the Jabberwocky  event the Paper Dragons existed in a  world of fantasy all contained within  the cardboard box when they first  emerged the message they left greeted  someone who had seemingly created the  box and its Fantastical contents or had  at least interacted with it before  possibly a particularly imaginative  child with the reality bending  capability to give life to the inanimate  Paper Dragons the origami creatures  seemed to mistake the foundation for  this original child rediscovering them  after an extended period of time they  made mention of the existence of other  mystical beings in their world including  Giants elves centaurs and more through  their subsequent messages it appeared  something about the world of  scp-1762 was gradually becoming unstable  though it required imagination to  sustain it to stabilize the fantasy  within the box but unfortunately the  foundation Personnel examining  scp-1762 refused to accept the existence  of this world they instead leaned on  science cold hard facts not The Whimsy  of the imaginary when opening the box  all they saw was its empty interior so  to them the fantasy wasn't real it was  the SCP foundation's own lack of belief  their refusal to make believe that was  gradually killing the world inside  scp-1762 through their notes still  unaware that they weren't speaking with  their child Creator the origami dragons  pleaded for Aid cries that fell on the  foundation's deaf ears within the Box  some magical war broke out between the  various creatures inside with the  survivors fleeing for their lives the  Box itself was effectively a portal  linking reality with this realm of  fantasy it existed in a time when the  myths and legends of old were  indeterminable  scp-1762 had once represented a physical  Bond a relationship between those two  worlds But as time had moved on belief  in legends in fantasy had all but  dwindled as the world inside the Box  fell into chaos becoming more and more  unstable the words hereby Dragons Were  burned away from the cardboard surface  in their final message the dragons  mentioned they hoped to escape to a new  world concluding with we are sad we love  you we will not forget you we are scared  will you forget us soon after the Box  returned to its original state with the  phrase here were dragons on the side  marking the end of the Jabberwocky event  and potentially the fantasy within  scp-1762 forever from mystical magical  tales of sadness we now turn to a sad  story from within the ranks of the  foundation itself as CP 451 formerly a  field agent working in the foundation  seems to an outside Observer to be  little more than an average man in his  30s while as average as someone working  for the foundation can be but let's turn  things around if we weren't to Look From  scp-451's perspective how would he see  us that's just the thing he wouldn't he  can't see us or anyone else for that  matter you see for a time this agent was  declared missing in action by the SCP  Foundation the last recorded assignment  he was sent on was an attempt to  retrieve a dangerous anomalous artifact  however this attempt ultimately failed  and scp-451 resurfaced a month later at  site 19. although from his point of view  the entire Foundation facility was empty  he was the last man on Earth or so he  thought at least some unknown influence  had permanently altered the agent's  perception he had been rendered  incapable of perceiving other human  beings now if you're a bit of a Hermit  who prefers their own company then this  might initially sound like like heaven  never having to experience another  awkward interaction with another person  like when you're walking down the street  and someone walking towards you and you  have to try to figure out which way  they're going so you can step in the  opposite direction and avoid bumping  into them then you inevitably do that  weird Shuffle when you both go to walk  the same way you know it's a whole thing  well as good as that might sound to be  rid of happenings like that imagine if  you couldn't see or hear anyone any  attempts the rest of the world made to  communicate with you not one of them  registering but it was somehow worse  than that thanks to his Newfound  surroundings or lack thereof  scp-451 believe that by interacting with  the anomalous artifact he had  single-handedly wiped out the entire  human race the guilt of that action  although only true from his perspective  weighed heavily on scp-451's conscience  he spent a lot of time wandering the  corridors of site 19 overwhelmed by his  apparent isolation eventually the  loneliness of his Newfound condition  coupled with the fallacious knowledge  that he had killed the entire human race  drove him to a state of near Madness but  there would be no escape from this new  state of Perpetual hell not only did the  condition appear to be incurable at  least from what he was capable of doing  but he would not even find solace in  death he had been cursed with some kind  of sadistic immortality and it seemed  like the only way to ever connect with  others was when they themselves were  near death as for what the foundation  were doing to help as CP 451 well  nothing there's little that can do to  reverse the change he was a valuable  field agent to them before it happened  and it's their hope that he can be again  if the process is somehow reversed until  then as CP 451 is forced to live out  this painful existence spending every  day as far as he can tell alone of  course if scp-451 could wish for  anything in his predicament it might be  something as simple as some company if  only there was an SCP that granted the  user their ultimate wish fulfilled any  Fantasy Made Them the hero of Their Own  Story while that happens to be the  function of scp-1230 it appears as a  green hardcover book with no discernible  labels on the spine nor on either front  or back covers the pages are almost  entirely blank save for one simple  phrase on the first one a hero is born  anyone that reads the pages of scp-1230  won't experience any effects immediately  in fact its anomalous properties don't  become apparent until the reader falls  asleep when they do they will experience  a vivid dream that can last anywhere  from 45 seconds to well let's just say  considerably longer although the reader  will never be asleep for any longer than  they normally would be in their dream  the reader will be the protagonist  within their own fantasy world the  entire time they remain fully aware of  their surroundings their senses and  faculties all work as they would as if  they were awake not unlike the fantasy  world of  scp-1762 the dream world's experience by  test subjects who read scp-1230 very  differently on the imagination of the  dreamer additionally once they re-emerge  from their Slumber they will be able to  recall all the events of the dream down  to every Last Detail every dream induced  by reading scp-1230 will also feature a  character known only as the bookkeeper a  friendly bearded old man in a green  cloak who is apparently the  personification of the book itself the  role of the bookkeeper seems to create  the fantasy Scapes as he calls them and  seemingly creates these bespoke worlds  on behalf of all the dreamers he  Encounters in accordance with their own  deepest desires and wants by now you're  no doubt thinking how could this  possibly be a sad SCP I bet you probably  even want to go with scp-1230 yourself  don't you and who wouldn't after all you  would get to be placed in a fantasy  Escape where you can do anything and  every everything you can think of on top  of that this isn't Inception dying or  being harmed in one of these dreams  doesn't translate to real world death  well not directly anyway remember when  we mention the dreams can last a  considerably long time at least in their  own internal fantasy Escape time well  here's what makes it one of the saddest  scps on this list maybe even ever  imagine getting to live out a fantasy  Adventure as the hero the main  protagonist in your own story picture  you spent a number of years in that  dream time experiencing every event of  that story that world first hand it  looks real it feels real for the time  that you're there at least so what  happens when you wake up how are you  going to feel if you're all of a sudden  pulled out of that fantasy and dropped  back into the mundanity of real life  would you prefer your fantasy to the  real world and what would you do if you  couldn't go back that was experience  firsthand by one of the foundation's  researchers known only as professor  he had specifically requested the  foundation to allow him to read scp-1230  and was giddy with excitement when it  came to be his turn like many others he  read the first page seeing a hero is  born and then instantly went to sleep  unwilling to wait until later clearly  eager to experience his very own fantasy  Escape Professor B was asleep for the  next 24 hours before the foundation  security Personnel were forced to  attempt to wake him up when he did he  looked around confused to be  unceremoniously returned to real life it  was almost as if the amount of time he  had spent within the bookkeeper's dream  world had caused him to momentarily  forget his old life with the foundation  however he soon regained his memory  after a brief reminder from fellow staff  but it was never the same after that  Professor B had experienced the life he  had always dreamed of within his dreams  and upon waking he had been returned to  a life where he was an aging tired man  and a dead-end job at the foundation he  was no hero here he was just another  nobody and the sadness was too much for  him professor B passed away not long  after after this tragedy the bookkeeper  was utterly distraught through the  medium of the book he left a note for  the Personnel of the SCP Foundation it  read I'm so sorry I never intended for  this to happen I just wanted to make  people happy a number of weeks passed  before the foundation was able to make  contact with the bookkeeper again  leaving a note that requested a  conversation with the entity a  foundation doctor experienced a dream  that was set in a Dark featureless Void  there he encountered the bookkeeper  crying to himself when questioned about  what had happened to Professor B the  embodiment of scp-1230 explained he had  such an active imagination I was able to  create a vast and beautiful Universe for  him and it was obvious that he wanted a  life like that for so long he conquered  foul beasts and rescued princesses they  built kingdoms and even raised a family  but he never wanted to  he delved so far into his fantasy world  that I soon realized he preferred his  dream over the real world I reminded him  that this was all merely an illusion but  he wouldn't listen to me I tried to keep  him happy for as long as I could  remember when we mentioned the dreams  can last a considerably long time at  least in their own internal fantasy  Escape time Professor B had been living  out his Ultimate Fantasy adventure for  200 years while only a full day's worth  of time had passed in the real world  having to live through all that only to  wake up and realize none of it was real  was perhaps too existentially  overwhelming for the professor then  again maybe he just preferred the world  of his fantasy Escape much more than the  world around him that brings us to one  of the most infamous anomalies in the  foundation's extensive history  scp-096 better known as the shy guy is a  terrifying towering creature with a  hairless body sunken eyes and a huge  gaping mouth but don't you ever get the  sense that there's something inherently  sad about  scp-096 insecurity is something a lot of  us experience and have to face every day  but the shy guys is taken to such an  extreme degree he can't bear the thought  of anyone looking at him it's so bad for  him that it causes him to experience so  much distress that he has to travel  lightning fast to anyone that looks at  his face and once he's caught up with  them and killed them then he's right  back to his usual routine sobbing and  weeping or pacing around his cell  perhaps his story isn't as sad as some  of the others on this list but we do  know it'd be a welcome change if someone  could make the shy guy smile just for a  little while now go check out 25 most  frightening scps and what is the  scariest SCP if you'd like to replace  that sadness with some good  old-fashioned fear

