the bookkeeper a  friendly bearded old man in a green  cloak who is apparently the  personification of the book itself the  role of the bookkeeper seems to create  the fantasy Scapes as he calls them and  seemingly creates these bespoke worlds  on behalf of all the dreamers he  Encounters in accordance with their own  deepest desires and wants by now you're  no doubt thinking how could this  possibly be a sad SCP I bet you probably  even want to go with scp-1230 yourself  don't you and who wouldn't after all you  would get to be placed in a fantasy  Escape where you can do anything and  every everything you can think of on top  of that this isn't Inception dying or  being harmed in one of these dreams  doesn't translate to real world death  well not directly anyway remember when  we mention the dreams can last a  considerably long time at least in their  own internal fantasy Escape time well  here's what makes it one of the saddest  scps on this list maybe even ever  imagine getting to live out a fantasy  Adventure as the hero the main  protagonist in your own story picture  you spent a number of years in that  dream time experiencing every event of  that story that world first hand it  looks real it feels real for the time  that you're there at least so what  happens when you wake up how are you  going to feel if you're all of a sudden  pulled out of that fantasy and dropped  back into the mundanity of real life  would you prefer your fantasy to the  real world and what would you do if you  couldn't go back that was experience  firsthand by one of the foundation's  researchers known only as professor  he had specifically requested the  foundation to allow him to read scp-1230  and was giddy with excitement when it  came to be his turn like many others he  read the first page seeing a hero is  born and then instantly went to sleep  unwilling to wait until later clearly  eager to experience his very own fantasy  Escape Professor B was asleep for the  next 24 hours before the foundation  security Personnel were forced to  attempt to wake him up when he did he  looked around confused to be  unceremoniously returned to real life it  was almost as if the amount of time he  had spent within the bookkeeper's dream  world had caused him to momentarily  forget his old life with the foundation  however he soon regained his memory  after a brief reminder from fellow staff  but it was never the same after that  Professor B had experienced the life he  had always dreamed of within his dreams  and upon waking he had been returned to  a life where he was an aging tired man  and a dead-end job at the foundation he  was no hero here he was just another  nobody and the sadness was too much for  him professor B passed away not long  after after this tragedy the bookkeeper  was utterly distraught through the  medium of the book he left a note for  the Personnel of the SCP Foundation it  read I'm so sorry I never intended for  this to happen I just wanted to make  people happy a number of weeks passed  before the foundation was able to make  contact with the bookkeeper again  leaving a note that requested a  conversation with the entity a  foundation doctor experienced a dream  that was set in a Dark featureless Void  there he encountered the bookkeeper  crying to himself when questioned about  what had happened to Professor B the  embodiment of scp-1230 explained he had  such an active imagination I was able to  create a vast and beautiful Universe for  him and it was obvious that he wanted a  life like that for so long he conquered  foul beasts and rescued princesses they  built kingdoms and even raised a family  but he never wanted to  he delved so far into his fantasy world  that I soon realized he preferred his  dream over the real world I reminded him  that this was all merely an illusion but  he wouldn't listen to me I tried to keep  him happy for as long as I could  remember when we mentioned the dreams  can last a considerably long time at  least in their own internal fantasy  Escape time Professor B had been living  out his Ultimate Fantasy adventure for  200 years while only a full day's worth  of time had passed in the real world  having to live through all that only to  wake up and realize none of it was real  was perhaps too existentially  overwhelming for the professor then  again maybe he just preferred the world  of his fantasy Escape much more than the  world around him that brings us to one  of the most infamous anomalies in the  foundation's extensive history  scp-096 better known as the shy guy is a  terrifying towering creature with a  hairless body sunken eyes and a huge  gaping mouth but don't you ever get the  sense that there's something inherently  sad about  scp-096 insecurity is something a lot of  us experience and have to face every day  but the shy guys is taken to such an  extreme degree he can't bear the thought  of anyone looking at him it's so bad for  him that it causes him to experience so  much distress that he has to travel  lightning fast to anyone that looks at  his face and once he's caught up with  them and killed them then he's right  back to his usual routine sobbing and  weeping or pacing around his cell  perhaps his story isn't as sad as some  of the others on this list but we do  know it'd be a welcome change if someone  could make the shy guy smile just for a  little while now go check out 25 most  frightening scps and what is the  scariest SCP if you'd like to replace  that sadness with some good  old-fashioned fear
 

